# tusd (uploads) on the batch-prod host: starvation of the NFS upload directory.
#
# The upload store is one flat NFS directory with millions of entries. A process
# that lists it (find, ls, du) holds the directory lock for every getdents(), which
# on NFS is a long chain of READDIRPLUS calls, and every tusd create/finish/delete
# waits behind it. 2026-09-18: two orphaned `find /` from an ssh session blocked
# 1,036 tusd threads for ~25 min (load average 1,049, CPU idle, NFS server fine).
#
# The probe reads /proc only, never the NFS mount. Status 1 = starved with a
# scanner present: kill it, and again every cycle one is still there. Status 2 =
# starved with nothing scanning: not this failure, so alert and touch nothing.
# The exec itself raises a monit event, so each kill is mailed with the culprit's
# command line in the description.
check program tusd-nfs-starvation with path "/etc/monit/scripts/tusd-nfs-starvation.sh" timeout 30 seconds
   group edge
   if status = 1 then exec "/etc/monit/scripts/tusd-nfs-starvation.sh --resolve" repeat every 1 cycles
   if status = 2 for 2 cycles then alert
